---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About — Lead From The Hip"
	description="David Morris on 28 years in HR and leader development, and why this site is built around the daily habit of doing rather than another framework."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="About"
		standfirst="I'm David Morris. I've spent 28 years in Human Resources, most of it helping leaders build and maintain high performing teams."
	>
		I got tired of knowing a lot about leadership<br />
		<span class="accent">and seeing little change in how I actually showed up.</span>
	</Hero>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">The short version</h2>
		<div class="measure flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink">
			<p>
				I've spent the last decade designing and facilitating leader
				development programs — from front-line supervisors to senior
				executives. Along the way, I've administered more assessments and
				360s than I can count, coached leaders through the debrief, and
				tried to help them figure out what to actually do with what they
				learned.
			</p>
			<p>
				That experience taught me something I didn't expect: the content
				was rarely the problem. Most leaders already have access to good
				material. Many have sat through solid programs, read the right
				books, and gotten accurate feedback. What's harder to find is a
				simple, repeatable structure for turning any of that into a daily
				habit.
			</p>
			<p>
				That's what this site is for. Not another framework. Not a program
				to roll out. Just a stripped-down approach to the part most of us
				skip — the doing.
			</p>
			<p>
				My background is in measurement. I spent the first seven years of
				my professional career analyzing jobs and designing tests to
				predict job performance. That instinct shapes everything here:
				don't assume something worked. Ask. Then ask again in ninety days,
				and let the answer be the answer.
			</p>
			<p>
				I built this because I kept watching smart, motivated people leave
				good programs and go right back to doing what they'd always done.
				Not because they didn't care — because no one gave them a structure
				small enough to actually use.
			</p>
			<p>This is my attempt at that structure.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">More about me</h2>
		<ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-1 text-ink">
			<li>
				M.S., Industrial-Organizational Psychology — California State University,
				San Bernardino (2001)
			</li>
			<li>Hogan Assessment Systems — certified in the HPI, HDS, and MVPI (2020)</li>
			<li>
				<a
					href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/david-c-morris-6b21a01"
					class="text-petrol underline hover:opacity-80 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
				>
					www.linkedin.com/in/david-c-morris-6b21a01
				</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">Get in touch</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure mb-6">
			The fastest route is a short call — twenty minutes — to work out
			whether there's anything here for you.
		</p>
		<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center">
			<a
				href="https://calendly.com/davidcmorris"
				class="bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				Book a call →
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
